==========================================================================
  APPENDIX J -- THE ADVERSARIAL PROTOCOL
  forcing applied to exhaustion makes an excluded sector
  unreachable, so no address is formed and discarded
==========================================================================

J.1  NO ADDRESS IS FORMED AND DISCARDED
     densities 2.0 to 8.0 including the hard threshold at 4.26;
     planted and unplanted, so unsatisfiable instances are included

       density  instances  discarded
           2.0        154          0
           3.0        154          0
           4.0        154          0
          4.26        154          0
           4.5        154          0
           5.0        154          0
           6.0        154          0
           8.0        154          0

    instances resolved: 1232; of which no address stands: 254

    PASS  no address formed and discarded across 1232 instances   [zero, by the mechanism rather than by stipulation]
    PASS  unsatisfiable instances are present, so the claim is not tested only where an address exists   [254 of 1232 carry no standing address]
    PASS  the hard threshold is exercised   [154 instances at density 4.26, 0 discarded]

J.2  PRODUCTION AGREES WITH THE COMPLETE TRUTH TABLE
     exhaustive over every address of the envelope.  The truth table
     is the verification device of resolution.py and is charged to
     no measure; it is what makes the agreement a proof rather than
     a sample.

    PASS  exact set equality against the truth table   600/600   [every instance]

J.3  THE CLOSURE RULE NEVER CLOSES A REGION HOLDING AN ADDRESS
     a region is closed when two boundaries force opposite
     orientations on one content.  Were that unsound, a standing
     address would be lost, and J.2 would have found it.

    PASS  no standing address was lost on any instance   [600 instances, exhaustive over each envelope]

J.4  THE RESIDUAL COMPONENT FACTORS AS THE PAPER STATES
     S_ij = 1/2 (s_i - s_j)(s_i + s_j - 2 s_c), exact rational
     arithmetic, exhaustive over all 2^k orientation states.
     Widths 3 to 7, so the even case the paper excludes from
     Theorem 8.4 is exercised rather than avoided.

        k  states   match  termini  predicted
        3       8       8        2          2
    PASS  k = 3: the closed form agrees on every orientation state   8/8
    PASS  k = 3: termini number 2, as predicted (2)   [2 for k odd; 2 + C(k, k/2) for k even]
        4      16      16        8          8
    PASS  k = 4: the closed form agrees on every orientation state   16/16
    PASS  k = 4: termini number 8, as predicted (8)   [2 for k odd; 2 + C(k, k/2) for k even]
        5      32      32        2          2
    PASS  k = 5: the closed form agrees on every orientation state   32/32
    PASS  k = 5: termini number 2, as predicted (2)   [2 for k odd; 2 + C(k, k/2) for k even]
        6      64      64       22         22
    PASS  k = 6: the closed form agrees on every orientation state   64/64
    PASS  k = 6: termini number 22, as predicted (22)   [2 for k odd; 2 + C(k, k/2) for k even]
        7     128     128        2          2
    PASS  k = 7: the closed form agrees on every orientation state   128/128
    PASS  k = 7: termini number 2, as predicted (2)   [2 for k odd; 2 + C(k, k/2) for k even]

