J.5  THE PROTOCOL CAN FAIL
     a protocol that cannot fail establishes nothing.  Each check
     below is a condition this protocol would report as a failure.

    PASS  the discard counter records a discard when one occurs   [so a zero in J.1 is a measurement, not an unincremented counter]
    PASS  a perturbed result set is reported unequal   [the comparison in J.2 is not an identity on its own argument]
    PASS  a wrong closed form is distinguished from the right one   [so J.4 compares two genuinely different expressions]

